  "notes": "Modified cash basis governmental funds (Total Governmental Funds column p5); business-type accrual (proprietary Totals column p7; disbursements 859,524 = operating 792,714 + interest 50,372 + debt issuance costs 16,438, printed as total business-type expenses on the Statement of Activities p2). Business-type roll-forward: 3,521,208 + 917,330 - 859,524 + contributed capital 833,507 = 4,412,521. Governmental roll-forward uses fund balances: 808,525 + 1,316,030 - 1,341,298 + 30,000 - 30,000 = 783,257 (Keno to General 27,000 and Streets 3,000). No single governmental cash total is printed (pooled cash, cash equivalents, county treasurer, CDs, restricted cash), so cash left null as in FY2023; CDs 311,632 in ending_investments. Proprietary debt proceeds (long-term 1,194,000, short-term 659,000) appear only in the cash flow statement p8. General Fund budget schedule 'Miscellaneous' 68,184 split using the p5 General Fund column (Miscellaneous 32,980 + Insurance proceeds 35,204). Capital outlay 119,482 (statement) and General Fund 46,782 have no printed function; Streets Fund capital outlay takes Streets/Highways from the fund. Budgeted transfers/debt proceeds with no actual are skipped. Balance sheet: governmental lines from p4 (totals 783,257 equal the government-wide governmental column p1), business-type from p1; component unit Ponderosa Villa excluded. Detail: General, Streets and Keno budgetary comparison schedules (Actual column, pp9-11); no business-type schedules. Read pages 1-11 of 11"
}
